toolUseResult.stdout:
  1	//! Phase-probed 1p/1c round-trip measurement cells over the
  2	//! zc-ring-x1 primitives.
  3	//!
  4	//! One **cell** is a main -> worker -> main round trip at a
  5	//! given ring flavor and thread placement, driven for a fixed
  6	//! duration. Each protocol phase is measured by its own
  7	//! [`TProbe`] and, on Linux, the cross-core cache-fill counters
  8	//! are collected in-process (no perf(1) needed):
  9	//!
 10	//! - `main send` / `worker send`: the producer's reserve +
 11	//!   fill + commit, including any stall acquiring peer-written
 12	//!   cache lines. The ring is never full here (one message in
 13	//!   flight, at any depth from 1 up), so no send ever waits
 14	//!   for space.
 15	//! - `worker recv` / `main recv`: the consumer's spin wait +
 16	//!   read + release. These absorb the in-flight half trip.
 17	//! - `... recv spin` / `... recv attempts`: the wait inside the
 18	//!   recv phase, decomposed: spin time (first failed attempt ->
 19	//!   reserve success) and the attempt count, recorded only for
 20	//!   reserves that actually waited.
 21	//!
 22	//! A **streaming cell** is the other shape: the producer sends
 23	//! a counter as fast as the ring admits for a fixed duration
 24	//! and the consumer drains it, the depth in play as slack, and
 25	//! the fill counters divided by the messages moved say how
 26	//! many lines crossed per message while streaming, the number
 27	//! the round-trip cell cannot give.
 28	//!
 29	//! The binaries:
 30	//!
 31	//! - `tp-cell` runs one cell and prints the probe reports.
 32	//! - `tp-matrix` runs every flavor × placement cell and emits
 33	//!   markdown tables.
 34	//! - `tp-stream` runs the streaming cell over the same matrix.
 35	
 36	use std::time::{Duration, Instant};
 37	
 38	use tp_runner::{LINE_BYTES, LineBuf, STOP, drive, pin_to_cpu, spin, unpin_current};
 39	use tprobe::TProbe;
 40	use tprobe::ticks;
 41	use zc_ring_x1::CACHE_LINE_SIZE;
 42	
 43	// The runner's line-aligned regions must be aligned the way
 44	// the rings want them.
 45	const _: () = assert!(LINE_BYTES == CACHE_LINE_SIZE);
