commit 4d31079f0e5669e6e3f99e9f03b5592274934703
Author: Wink Saville <wink@saville.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 10 09:38:54 2026 -0700

    feat: mpsc v1 in the tools, flavors named xpsc-vN

    The measurement tools and the demo sweep know four ring flavors, and the
    MPSC one is a concrete function on the crate's default re-export, so the
    new mpsc::v1 has no way in and no depth-1 cell anywhere. Two of the four
    flavors also go by bare names, spsc and mpsc, which mean v0 only by a rule
    a reader has to know.

    * The MPSC cell, stream, and demo loops are bound to one version.
      - Each becomes a macro stamped per version by module path, as the SPSC
        ones are, and mpsc-v1 joins as a fifth flavor with a depth floor of 1.
    * The bare names spsc and mpsc stand for v0.
      - Every flavor is named xpsc-vN in the tools' arguments and labels, and
        the recorded tables' columns follow.

